# Quicksave — /bughunt on UnitySolarSystem: 5 bugs found and fixed, working tree unreviewed by user yet
_Printed: 2026-10-12_

## Current task
Just finished running `/bughunt` (no time budget — exhaustive single pass) across the whole
tracked codebase plus the 3 new untracked files. Found and fixed 5 real bugs, verified with the
Core.Tests suite (165/165 passing). **Nothing has been committed.** The user has not yet reviewed
or approved the fixes in the working tree — next step on resume is to wait for the user's
reaction (they may want changes, a commit, or further investigation) rather than assuming the
hunt is fully "done and accepted."

## Decisions locked this session
- Bughunt scope: all tracked C# source (74 files) + 3 untracked in-progress files
  (`PilotFlight.cs`, `PilotFlightTests.cs`, `ModelViewer.cs`) — these were explicitly included
  since they're real in-progress work, not generated/vendored code.
- Combat `Repair()` bug: fixed by splitting hull/subsystem repair (scaled by share) from a new
  `FreeResupply()` method (full ammo/crew/marine reset) — ships now only get costed resupply via
  `War.Refit()`'s existing gated logic; platforms (no costed path) call both `Repair()` and
  `FreeResupply()` from `RebuildPlatforms()`.
- Economy bug: fixed by multiplying input consumption by `efficiency` (not just `run`) in
  `Economy.Produce()`, so non-limiting input shortages no longer waste plentiful inputs.
- InputState bugs: fixed `MouseDelta` not being cleared in `Reset()` (caused runaway piloting
  rotation on device-null frames), and fixed the scroll-wheel normalization discontinuity (was
  snapping small raw deltas straight to a full ±1 notch).
- ModelViewer bug: **root cause found, not a Frame Debugger mystery.** The project renders
  camera-relative (`SolarSystemApp.UpdateClipPlanes` pins the camera at `Vector3.zero`;
  `SolarSystemApp.Relative(scene) = scene - cameraPosition`), so all live scene geometry is always
  drawn clustered near world-origin — exactly where ModelViewer's own instantiated model and
  camera also sit. ModelViewer only ever disabled *other cameras*; it never restricted its own
  camera's `cullingMask`, so it was rendering the live scene's nearby geometry too. Fixed by adding
  a dedicated `ModelViewer` Unity layer (slot 31, previously unused — see
  `ProjectSettings/TagManager.asset`) and restricting the viewer's camera + light + instantiated
  model (recursively) to that layer.
- ModelViewer.cs and InputState.cs changes can't be compiled/tested outside Unity (the standalone
  `Tests/SolarSystem.Core.csproj` only compiles `Assets/SolarSystem/Core/**`, not `Runtime/**`) —
  verified by hand-reading, not by a build. Worth opening in the Unity editor to confirm visually,
  especially the ModelViewer fix (toggle with `V` key, or `-modelviewer <name>` on the command
  line).

